1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,863
A worrying spot. A specialist far away.

2
00:00:02,863 --> 00:00:06,900
OncoScan's promise: an answer within twenty-four hours.

3
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:09,382
This is the working prototype.

4
00:00:09,382 --> 00:00:13,243
A patient signs in, picks skin or mouth, and adds photos.

5
00:00:13,243 --> 00:00:16,224
Each photo is checked for darkness and blur.

6
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:20,627
They describe it, confirm cover, and send. The case clock starts.

7
00:00:20,627 --> 00:00:23,878
The specialist sees the case first in the queue,

8
00:00:23,878 --> 00:00:26,453
marks it suspicious, and signs a note.

9
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:29,569
The patient gets the result and the next step.

10
00:00:30,019 --> 00:00:33,150
The whole loop runs in the browser, with no server.

11
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:35,729
It passed five out of five automated runs.

12
00:00:35,729 --> 00:00:39,107
The photo check caught a dark and a blurred test image.

13
00:00:39,557 --> 00:00:44,573
It targets two bottlenecks from the brief: late detection and slow referral.

14
00:00:44,573 --> 00:00:48,929
No AI model is connected yet. Scores on demo cases are examples.

15
00:00:49,379 --> 00:00:52,285
OncoScan. Know within twenty-four hours.
